WEBVTT

00:15.120 --> 00:21.080
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON

01:32.240 --> 01:37.580
#36: EMBRACING YOUR AMBITIONS
IN THE LIGHT PART 1

02:05.480 --> 02:06.310
UNIQUE MONSTER
Encountered Lycagon the Nightslayer.

02:06.310 --> 02:08.110
LYCAGON THE NIGHTSLAYER ENCOUNTERED
Encountered Lycagon the Nightslayer.

02:09.110 --> 02:11.320
I had this thought
in the corner of my mind.

02:12.240 --> 02:14.320
That I only lost to Lycagon

02:14.990 --> 02:20.620
because I was new to SLF and lacked
the experience and level for it.

02:26.040 --> 02:27.790
Talk about kidding myself.

02:32.050 --> 02:37.000
The deadly presence
that exudes out of her...

02:37.970 --> 02:40.970
...is nothing as straightforward as that.

02:45.850 --> 02:46.980
SF-Zoo!

02:48.400 --> 02:49.770
All members, start the action!

02:50.210 --> 02:52.530
We're using the "Anti-Dragon" tactic!

02:52.530 --> 02:54.030
Roger!

02:54.030 --> 02:55.240
Let's go!

03:04.710 --> 03:07.750
Sunraku, what should we do?

03:07.750 --> 03:10.500
Just stay out of our way and watch.

03:10.500 --> 03:13.840
Just watch what we can do
when we're serious!

03:14.920 --> 03:16.300
Yeah.

03:16.760 --> 03:21.260
They even researched Lycagon's behavior
patterns and located where she'll show up.

03:21.890 --> 03:26.020
Let's see if they're really something more
than just a group of animal fanatics.

03:48.550 --> 03:50.630
What are they doing?

03:50.630 --> 03:54.300
Equipping two Tower Shields like that?
How are they supposed to move?

03:55.470 --> 03:57.130
Enhance Durability!

03:57.130 --> 03:57.800
Okay!

03:57.800 --> 03:58.550
Yes!

03:59.680 --> 04:02.560
ENHANCE DURABILITY

04:02.560 --> 04:04.810
All right! We're buffed to the limit!

04:05.230 --> 04:06.600
Let's do this!

04:09.270 --> 04:11.980
Looks like they're using skill assists
to gain some mobility.

04:11.980 --> 04:13.020
TANK, PLAYERS WHO PLAY THE ROLE OF ATTRACTING
Five tanks,

04:13.020 --> 04:14.070
ENEMY'S ATTACK TO PROTECT THEIR ALLIES
Five tanks,

04:14.070 --> 04:14.730
ENEMY'S ATTACK TO PROTECT THEIR ALLIES
and 10 debuffers

04:14.730 --> 04:15.940
DEBUFFER, PLAYERS WHO PLAY THE ROLE
including Animalia herself.

04:15.940 --> 04:17.150
OF APPLYING DEBUFF ON ENEMIES
including Animalia herself.

04:17.150 --> 04:17.990
OF APPLYING DEBUFF ON ENEMIES

04:17.990 --> 04:20.740
They completely abandon
any real means of attack.

04:20.740 --> 04:22.990
What an extreme setup.

04:39.630 --> 04:41.890
Bring it on, Lycagon!

04:49.850 --> 04:52.270
Even with all of those defense buffs,

04:52.270 --> 04:55.270
I still take this much
damage from one hit!

04:57.190 --> 04:59.280
Don't let her hit again!
Prepare for impact!

05:02.890 --> 05:04.870
What a fast attack.

05:04.870 --> 05:08.150
Even without all this gear,
we'd never be able to evade that!

05:08.150 --> 05:10.040
We're fine if it doesn't instantly kill us!

05:10.040 --> 05:12.170
Don't let it get to you
and fall outta formation!

05:12.550 --> 05:15.670
I see. They got a nice teamwork.

05:15.670 --> 05:18.550
Those metal boulders are pretty skilled.

05:18.550 --> 05:19.380
Yes.

05:19.730 --> 05:22.390
Not only do they attract her attack...

05:26.060 --> 05:29.090
They also shift around to keep Lycagon
from moving as much as possible.

05:29.090 --> 05:30.060
C'mon, what's wrong!

05:36.650 --> 05:39.690
So that their debuffers can
land their spells more easily.

05:40.280 --> 05:42.950
First team, fire!

05:42.950 --> 05:44.200
Atlas Bind!

05:44.490 --> 05:46.780
ATLAS BIND

05:55.290 --> 05:57.090
Okay! Two of them hit!

06:07.600 --> 06:10.100
No way! In just one bite?!

06:10.100 --> 06:11.100
Stay firm!

06:11.100 --> 06:13.810
Second team, keep it raining!

06:13.810 --> 06:14.730
Yes, Ma'am!

06:14.730 --> 06:16.560
Atlas Bind!

06:24.910 --> 06:26.570
All right, we got her!

06:28.200 --> 06:30.370
She will tear the spells apart!

06:30.830 --> 06:33.210
Applying buff magic!

06:39.880 --> 06:43.090
Whoa! They're doing pretty well!

06:43.090 --> 06:47.350
That's SF-Zoo's standard strategy
that can even capture dragons.

06:49.220 --> 06:53.010
They've got the best tanks in SLF
soaking up all the attacks...

06:53.010 --> 06:55.730
...and use numerous debuffs
to hold their target down.

06:57.690 --> 06:59.210
And as a finisher...

07:05.740 --> 07:08.450
A unique shamanistic spell
that can only be used

07:08.450 --> 07:10.080
when I equip this Unique Weapon,

07:10.080 --> 07:11.700
UNDERWORLD KEYSTAFF
"Underworld Keystaff"...

07:16.250 --> 07:18.630
Grab it with your dark hand...

07:18.630 --> 07:20.960
Hands of Tartarus!

07:22.960 --> 07:25.970
HANDS OF TARTARUS

07:33.850 --> 07:34.930
Wow!

07:34.930 --> 07:36.100
She got her!

07:36.100 --> 07:41.610
It inflicts immobility aliment on
all living things for one minute.

07:42.150 --> 07:43.370
And with this...

07:43.860 --> 07:49.530
Our operation to fully capture Lycagon
the Nightslayer is a complete success!

07:49.530 --> 07:50.660
Yay!

07:50.660 --> 07:52.660
Yaaaay!

07:52.660 --> 07:54.120
Yay!

07:54.120 --> 07:56.500
Wow! I gotta screenshot
this to commemorate!

07:56.500 --> 07:57.790
- Me too!
- Same!

07:57.790 --> 08:00.130
C'mon, guys. We've got no time for that.

08:01.250 --> 08:05.590
Our objective is to trigger
the Unique Scenario!

08:05.590 --> 08:06.420
Yes!

08:06.420 --> 08:08.260
But send me those pictures later!

08:08.260 --> 08:09.930
- Okay!
- Sure!

08:10.840 --> 08:14.560
Seems like they'll fulfill
the requirement at this rate.

08:14.560 --> 08:19.940
Well, I'm sorry to disappoint them,
but I don't think that'll happen.

08:20.900 --> 08:23.900
The information that
Pencilgon told her...

08:24.330 --> 08:28.950
"By landing a total of 100 critical hits
on Lycagon the Nightslayer,

08:28.950 --> 08:33.490
you will get an invite from Rabitz
which will trigger the Unique Scenario."

08:33.880 --> 08:36.200
...is not entirely accurate.

08:36.830 --> 08:38.500
Or rather...

08:38.500 --> 08:42.380
There is a high chance that your weapon
and level have something to do with it.

08:42.380 --> 08:44.300
And Vorpal Soul...

08:44.300 --> 08:47.050
I don't know for sure
what that is exactly,

08:47.630 --> 08:53.430
but I doubt Boss Vash would applaud
the act of ganging up to beat one target.

08:53.430 --> 08:55.890
In short, Pencilgon...

08:55.890 --> 09:00.270
- I'm debt free! Yay!
- She ripped Animalia off with true,

09:00.270 --> 09:00.640
but incomplete information.

09:00.640 --> 09:02.770
I'M DEBT FREE~♪
but incomplete information.

09:02.770 --> 09:04.690
SO HEARTLESS
So heartless...

09:05.230 --> 09:08.610
- I'm debt free! Yay!
- But well, the things I told her

09:08.610 --> 09:10.700
- I'm debt free! Yay!
- are uncertain at best, anyway.

09:12.280 --> 09:13.700
But still...

09:14.170 --> 09:17.830
To be honest, I was not expecting
SF-Zoo to make it this far.

09:17.830 --> 09:21.920
To think they can completely
bind Lycagon like that.

09:22.750 --> 09:24.210
And yet...

09:24.750 --> 09:29.130
The wolf herself sure seems
to not look all that bothered.

09:31.760 --> 09:36.970
You still have something
up your sleeve, don't you?

10:03.500 --> 10:06.000
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON

10:07.000 --> 10:09.510
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON

10:14.890 --> 10:21.100
Now then, let's find out
what Lycagon the Nightslayer's fur feels like!

10:42.710 --> 10:44.040
What's the matter?

10:44.830 --> 10:47.040
I had all this wrong.

10:48.210 --> 10:51.840
I thought Lycagon was the "Nightslayer"
because she attacked by night.

10:52.970 --> 10:55.340
Something in the sky...

10:55.340 --> 10:57.470
But that wasn't the case...

11:03.350 --> 11:04.480
Somebody...

11:05.100 --> 11:07.310
No, the "night"...

11:08.980 --> 11:10.730
...is looking at me?

11:14.070 --> 11:16.280
What's attacking you
is the darkness.

11:16.280 --> 11:17.990
The "night" itself.

11:17.990 --> 11:20.490
The advancing darkness of night...

11:20.490 --> 11:22.410
...is "Lycagon the Nightslayer"!

11:34.210 --> 11:36.180
W-What was that?!

11:36.180 --> 11:37.130
An attack?!

11:38.180 --> 11:39.890
No way...

11:39.890 --> 11:43.680
Lycagon shouldn't be able to move
because of our leader's shamanistic spell!

11:55.570 --> 11:56.820
No way...

11:56.820 --> 11:59.450
W-Why...

12:00.070 --> 12:02.660
...is there another Lycagon?!

12:04.970 --> 12:06.790
Sunraku... is that...

12:07.460 --> 12:09.420
A second Lycagon...

12:10.040 --> 12:12.750
No... her clone?

12:15.340 --> 12:16.550
Leader!

12:17.550 --> 12:19.930
L-Lycagon!

12:21.010 --> 12:24.890
Animals are cute and brave,

12:24.890 --> 12:27.640
and their difference from us
is what makes them so precious.

12:27.640 --> 12:30.400
We gotta rescue her!
Get back in formation!

12:32.440 --> 12:34.060
Leader!

12:35.570 --> 12:39.700
As someone who's seriously
allergic to animals in real life,

12:39.700 --> 12:43.530
Down to the details of the fleas
in the fur of animal monsters,

12:43.530 --> 12:47.790
Shangri-La Frontier is a game that
is so infinitely close to reality...

12:47.790 --> 12:52.500
...that it was truly like a Shangri-La;
a paradise for me.

12:52.500 --> 12:55.000
I adore everything
about these animals...

12:55.000 --> 12:58.340
I've loved and interacted
with them more than anyone.

13:05.260 --> 13:07.600
That's why I can tell.

13:07.600 --> 13:09.310
Lycagon the Nightslayer...

13:10.350 --> 13:12.690
She's different...

13:12.690 --> 13:14.270
W-Wait!

13:20.450 --> 13:22.030
Leader!

13:27.370 --> 13:28.250
She's gone!

13:28.250 --> 13:30.080
It must've been some kind of skill!

13:30.080 --> 13:31.290
Watch out!

13:31.290 --> 13:34.710
Watch out?! Watch for what?!

13:34.710 --> 13:36.750
Anyway, don't lower your guard!

13:40.920 --> 13:42.300
Her clone...

13:42.300 --> 13:43.930
She moved in an instant!

13:44.970 --> 13:46.350
She's gone again!

13:46.350 --> 13:47.680
She's not simply moving...

13:48.140 --> 13:49.930
She's traveling through the darkness.

13:50.750 --> 13:51.770
Behind you!

13:58.150 --> 14:00.900
Not only that, but she also
becomes "one" in the darkness.

14:01.570 --> 14:05.660
The invisible attack carried out
by her clone that melts into the darkness.

14:07.910 --> 14:10.000
What did it just do to me?

14:10.830 --> 14:12.460
What did it hit me with?

14:13.580 --> 14:18.340
So that's your secret,
Lycagon the Nightslayer!

14:45.410 --> 14:47.240
I-I can't do this! Help—

14:50.160 --> 14:53.250
SF-Zoo was wiped out in an instant.

14:53.250 --> 14:55.250
What should we do, Sunraku?

14:55.750 --> 15:00.800
Thanks to them, we've had an encounter
with Lycagon the Nightslayer.

15:00.800 --> 15:05.010
And we've got a chance to closely watch
her previously unpredictable attacks.

15:06.050 --> 15:12.720
Namely, we've got the one-in-a-million
chance to teach that smug pup a lesson.

15:13.310 --> 15:14.100
Very well.

15:15.020 --> 15:16.020
So we'll do it, huh?

15:18.730 --> 15:22.230
But there's one big issue.

15:25.360 --> 15:28.160
If we take on Lycagon like this,

15:28.160 --> 15:33.410
there's a chance Psyger-0 will trigger
the flag for the EX Unique Scenario.

15:33.410 --> 15:35.250
Is there something that matters?

15:35.830 --> 15:38.250
Information is a powerful weapon.

15:38.920 --> 15:41.500
Not to mention, Psyger-0's clan...

15:42.210 --> 15:47.130
Schwarz Vulf craves intel on Lycagon
the Nightslayer more than anything.

15:47.840 --> 15:51.930
It could heavily affect
the power balance of our clan alliance.

15:54.770 --> 15:57.850
I can't underestimate
the power of veteran players.

15:58.600 --> 16:01.060
Even with SF-Zoo's
unbalanced party structure,

16:01.060 --> 16:03.860
they succeeded in
binding Lycagon down.

16:04.860 --> 16:09.990
If Schwarz Vulf were to obtain the info
and form an appropriate party,

16:09.990 --> 16:12.620
there's no guarantee they
wouldn't kill Lycagon with it.

16:13.200 --> 16:17.290
They'd have a monopoly on
the resulting EX Unique Scenario.

16:17.290 --> 16:21.710
And if that happens, they'd be the first
to beat Lycagon the Nightslayer for good.

16:21.710 --> 16:23.630
I must avoid that at all costs.

16:25.630 --> 16:30.340
Psyger-0 has already seen
what Lycagon's clone can do.

16:30.340 --> 16:33.600
It's too risky to let them learn more.

16:34.260 --> 16:37.810
Which means my current
best course of action

16:39.020 --> 16:41.690
is to get both of us wiped up,

16:41.690 --> 16:44.650
even if it means dragging
Psyger-0 down with me!

16:46.320 --> 16:49.860
Dying on purpose after running
into a Unique Monster?

16:51.160 --> 16:54.660
I'm the one who invited them,
and that's what I do?

16:56.290 --> 16:58.500
Not only it's a bad manner,

16:58.500 --> 17:01.750
but doing that will also put my character
as a gamer into question.

17:01.750 --> 17:04.590
Even ignoring that,
it's just a lame thing to do!

17:05.630 --> 17:10.550
Dammit! And I must make it
to Fifticia by tomorrow morning!

17:10.550 --> 17:15.180
If I have to die and redo all the travel,
I've got no time to waste over this!

17:15.720 --> 17:17.560
I've got to decide now!

17:18.100 --> 17:20.520
That's the best path for me right now!

17:21.560 --> 17:23.810
Sunraku?

17:25.020 --> 17:28.490
What's wrong?
He's not acting like himself.

17:29.030 --> 17:32.070
Normally, Hizutome would be more...

17:34.240 --> 17:39.630
The first time I saw Hizutome
was on a rainy day.

17:48.840 --> 17:51.340
His bright smile caught my attention.

17:52.550 --> 17:55.850
And I wanted to know
what made him smile like that.

18:02.980 --> 18:06.190
With the game in his hands,

18:06.190 --> 18:10.110
he was smiling as if he had uncovered
some precious jewel or a treasure.

18:18.490 --> 18:21.500
I was attracted to that sight of him...

18:23.000 --> 18:29.210
And it made me want to talk to him someday,
even if it's inside a game.

18:30.670 --> 18:33.800
And yet, even though that "jewel"
is in front of him right now,

18:33.800 --> 18:37.390
Hizutome is not trying to
grab it with all his might.

18:38.430 --> 18:42.640
Something is getting in the way of Hizutome
from moving his legs forward.

18:43.310 --> 18:46.730
Is there anything I can do for him?

18:50.150 --> 18:52.280
Umm, Sunraku.

18:52.280 --> 18:54.700
Huh? Y-Yes?

18:54.700 --> 19:01.080
Um, to be honest,
unlike other members of Schwarz Vulf,

19:01.080 --> 19:04.790
I don't have that much fixation
on Lycagon the Nightslayer.

19:06.040 --> 19:08.170
I want to beat her someday,

19:08.170 --> 19:10.670
but simply because
she's an in-game monster.

19:10.670 --> 19:15.300
Sometimes I even think,
"So what if she beats me?"

19:16.300 --> 19:20.310
But whenever I feel like that...

19:20.890 --> 19:23.810
I will recall Hizutome's smile...

19:23.810 --> 19:27.560
I make up one thing in my mind.

19:27.560 --> 19:28.920
Since I'm doing this...

19:30.150 --> 19:33.000
I'll have fun with it
with everything I've got.

19:36.490 --> 19:38.490
It's not about winning or losing.

19:38.490 --> 19:42.830
Right now, at this very moment,
let's enjoy this game to the fullest!

19:45.830 --> 19:50.090
Playing the game seriously...
What's wrong with that?

19:50.090 --> 19:54.010
Everything is fun
when you do it seriously.

19:56.130 --> 19:58.590
Enjoy it to the fullest...

20:12.020 --> 20:14.110
Yeah, you're right.

20:15.320 --> 20:16.860
Sorry, Rei.

20:19.160 --> 20:22.120
Did I look that bored to you?

20:22.120 --> 20:24.830
Huh? N-No, I mean...

20:24.830 --> 20:27.870
Good grief. All that about
clans, monopolies...

20:28.240 --> 20:30.500
And I nearly try to get
myself killed on purpose?

20:30.960 --> 20:33.380
Why am I thinking like a coward?

20:33.380 --> 20:35.630
What the hell am I even
fighting this game for?!

20:38.550 --> 20:40.390
Yeah, right!

20:41.930 --> 20:46.680
If I'm having fun right now,
who cares what comes next!

20:49.270 --> 20:51.900
Thinking about the future is nice and all,

20:51.900 --> 20:55.280
but why make the present
boring because of that?

20:56.570 --> 20:58.900
Thanks, Rei.

21:02.490 --> 21:04.030
You opened my eyes.

21:04.410 --> 21:06.910
Let's do this, with everything we've got!

21:08.290 --> 21:13.290
SUNRAKU SENT YOU A PARTY REQUEST ACCEPT?
NO - YES

21:15.250 --> 21:16.050
Yes!

21:42.200 --> 21:45.740
Schwarz Vulf will get intel on Lycagon?

21:45.740 --> 21:47.740
Who the hell gives a crap about that!

21:47.740 --> 21:52.580
We just have to beat her
right here and now, and it's all good!

21:53.020 --> 21:55.340
Prepare yourself, Lycagon the Nightslayer!

21:55.340 --> 21:58.340
I'm nothing like the last time!

21:58.340 --> 22:03.760
I'll show you the power
of a level-99 player!
